.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt SACC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sacc
.Nd send one command to sad
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends
.Ar command
and its arguments as one line to the
.Xr sad 1
socket with
.Xr socat 1
and prints the reply.
.Pp
For
.Cm add ,
.Nm
sends one
.Cm add
line per path and converts each path, including Windows paths,
to an absolute Cygwin path with
.Xr cygpath 1 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SAD_SOCK
Socket path.
Default:
.Pa /tmp/sad-sock .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when no command is given; otherwise it exits with the status of
.Xr socat 1 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sacc add 'C:\eUsers\eme\eMusic\esong.mp3'
$ sacc play
$ sacc status playback
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sad 1
